.TH "SPGEN-READ_MODEL" "1" "" "spgen 0.1.0" ""
.SH NAME
spgen\-read_model \- Generates the shared read model with its changesets
.SH SYNOPSIS
mix sp.gen.read_model [options] <READ\-MODEL>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The queryable projection of the events. Typed Ecto schema plus the changesets the projections need.
.SH Prerequisite
.IP \[bu] 2
The Domain Model (../../../../domain\-model/README.md) contains the read model's schema, its projections, and the aggregate invariants that make a field unique.
.SH "What the generator does"
use TypedEctoSchema, import Ecto.Changeset, @primary_key (id, not autogenerated), @timestamps_opts in microsecond precision, @schema_prefix from the subdomain, the typed_schema fields from the model's schema with the mapped Ecto types, timestamps(), and insert_changeset/2 plus update_changeset/2 casting the fields they need — with a unique_constraint(:<field>) for every unique\-field invariant.
.PP
The @moduledoc describes what the read model represents, from the model's projection rules.
.SH "Left to you"
.IP \[bu] 2
The table: mix ecto.gen.migration, including the unique index a unique_constraint needs (migration (./migration.md)).
.IP \[bu] 2
A custom changeset, only when insert_changeset/update_changeset cannot express the projection.
.SH Tests
No test file of its own: the read model is tested where it is written — the projector (./projector.md) cases in the event test (./event\-test.md) — and where it is read, in the operation test (./operation\-test.md).
.SS "Generated files"
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/read_model.ex (Ecto schema with both changesets)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-subdomain\fR \fI<SUBDOMAIN>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-composite\fR \fI<COMPOSITE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-constituent\fR \fI<CONSTITUENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
model root, default docs/domain\-model (relative to \-\-root)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
repo root, default inferred from the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
report the drift, write nothing
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
FE: rewrite present generated units in place
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIREAD\-MODEL\fR>
the element: esdm: reference, *.esdm.yaml, kind.name, or bare name
.SH "SEE ALSO"
spgen(1)
suites: operation, feature
